From: erosqcfw <erosqcfw@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] MusicChunk: 16 KiB chunks (4x fewer player/decoder wakeups)

Every full MusicChunk makes the decoder thread signal the player thread
(DecoderBridge::FlushChunk -> client_cond), and the player wakes, moves
the chunk towards the outputs and sleeps again.  With 4 KiB chunks a
44.1 kHz/16-bit stream does that ~45x/s (~90x/s for 24-bit), each a pair
of context switches that also preempts the decoder on this single-core
X1000.  16 KiB chunks cut system context switches during wired FLAC
playback ~60% (EROS Q, measured 5500-7000 -> ~2450 per 30 s).

The pipe still holds the same number of bytes (audio_buffer_size is
divided by CHUNK_SIZE), so RAM use does not change.  Two chunk-count
thresholds are kept in bytes: the player's output-pipe high-water mark
(64 chunks = 256 KiB at 4 KiB -> 64 * 4096 / CHUNK_SIZE) and the erosq
paused read-ahead floor from 0002 (16 chunks = 64 KiB -> 64 KiB /
CHUNK_SIZE).

---
--- a/src/MusicChunk.hxx
+++ b/src/MusicChunk.hxx
@@ -17,7 +17,7 @@
 #include <memory>
 #include <span>
 
-static constexpr size_t CHUNK_SIZE = 4096;
+static constexpr size_t CHUNK_SIZE = 16384;
 
 struct AudioFormat;
 struct Tag;
--- a/src/player/Thread.cxx
+++ b/src/player/Thread.cxx
@@ -950,7 +950,7 @@
 inline bool
 Player::PlayNextChunk() noexcept
 {
-	if (!pc.LockWaitOutputConsumed(64))
+	if (!pc.LockWaitOutputConsumed(64 * 4096 / CHUNK_SIZE))
 		/* the output pipe is still large enough, don't send
 		   another chunk */
 		return true;
@@ -1128,7 +1128,7 @@
 			   paused (~1 s of audio); lift it and wake the
 			   decoder as soon as playback resumes */
 			const unsigned limit = paused && !decoder_starting
-				? (buffer_before_play > 16U ? buffer_before_play : 16U)
+				? std::max(buffer_before_play, unsigned(64 * 1024 / CHUNK_SIZE))
 				: 0U;
 			if (dc.pause_chunk_limit != limit) {
 				dc.pause_chunk_limit = limit;
